<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ICS half yr shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>ICS half yr shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - net profit	    208.2	 vs 161.0</p>
<p>    - headline		190.7	 vs 157.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 36.0	  vs 30.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   79.94	 vs 61.74</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   129.52	vs 90.97</p>
<p>    Tax			 40.35	 vs 29.74</p>
<p>    Interest received     2.95	  vs 3.78</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,614.36    vs 1,435.34</p>
<p>Div payable July 8</p>
<p>on register May 30</p>
<p>Full name: ICS Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  5.83	  vs 7.81</p>
<p>    Abnormal profit	 7.94	  vs none</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the abnormal profit stemmed from the profit on the sale of discontinued operations and on disposal of land and buildings.</p>
<p>They said that although they did not see any fundamental change in consumer demand, the coninuing focus on efficiencies and value added products should enable the group to show satisfactory growth for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
